This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   This is an unattended, scheduled Claudinite work-item execution (not an interactive chat session). The session was fired automatically per `engine/scheduler/queue/instructions.md`'s procedure, targeting GitHub issue `missingbulb/Claudinite#1280` (invocation nonce `1280-ppjcdck7`), which dispatches the `canon-curation/growth-promote` task. No human has typed anything into this conversation; all "instructions" come from the stored task file and the issue's Context field, which is binding scope and must never be widened.

   The task (per `.claudinite/local/packs/canon-curation/tasks/growth-promote/task.md`): read the **local packs** (RULES.md prose + coded check `.mjs` modules only — never task scripts, code comments, product source, or config) of exactly these 10 target member repos named in issue #1280's Context: `missingbulb/ClaudiniteWebsite`, `missingbulb/CrosswordChat`, `missingbulb/EdFringeNow`, `missingbulb/GoogleCalendarEventCreator`, `missingbulb/LaughCounter`, `missingbulb/Shepherd`, `missingbulb/ShoutsAndWhispers`, `missingbulb/TLDR`, `missingbulb/VascularColoring`, `missingbulb/WIP`. For each candidate lesson: generalize it (strip project specifics) BEFORE judging worthiness; judge worthiness against `.claudinite/local/packs/canon-curation/item-routing.md`'s bar (distilled, portable to a *future* project, durable, readable through its channel, not already covered ANYWHERE in the whole corpus — default to reject when unsure, but lean inclusive on narrow-but-real items); descend the promotion ladder (check > skill > prose, prose is fallback not default); route each surviving prose item to exactly one existing owning file, or — only for a technology with zero existing pack home — mint a brand-new stub pack in its OWN separate Py PR. Open a PR against Claudinite's `main` for the lesson-promotion changes (write surface bounded to `packs/`/`skills/` only, CI-enforced), bump every touched pack's `version` + add a `VERSIONS.md` row in the same change, log the run as a dated comment on tracker issue **#99** ("Claudinite tracker: Promote to Canon"), then converge work item #1280 via `converge-item.mjs` and run `session-end-command.mjs`. The standing bound: execute ONLY this one item, never touch/fix other stuck work (I found 3 other open unmerged growth-promote PRs — #1021, #1157, #1204 — and correctly left them alone while using them only to avoid duplicating their content).

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Claudinite's growth lifecycle: EXTRACT (per-member, auto-merge) → PROMOTE (this task, central, human-reviewed PR) → DEDUP (per-member).
   - The promotion ladder: platform setting → hook → check → skill → prose (prose is the fallback, never the default).
   - Item-routing worthiness bar: Distilled / Portable (future-project test) / Durable-reusable / Readable-through-its-channel / Not-already-covered-anywhere.
   - Canon pack structure: `packs/<id>/pack.mjs` (manifest with `version`, `minEngineVersion`, `ruleRoutingGuidance`, etc.), `RULES.md` (prose, indexed by README), `VERSIONS.md` (bump log), `README.md` (rule-index + check-index tables, machine-verified by `engine-tests/rule-index.test.mjs`), `worldRules/*.mjs` (whole-repo-scope checks, auto-discovered by directory), `workRules/*.mjs` (work/diff-scoped checks, auto-discovered by directory, typically declare `scope: 'work'`), `test/pack.test.mjs` (tests for both).
